waited dinner."},{"day":2,"title":"From the Blue Fire of Ijen to the Golden Sunset of Papuma","summary":"Today was a mix of extreme adventure and relaxation. We began with a climb to Ijen, followed by lunch to recharge. Afterward, we headed south to the coast to close the day with a sunset at Papuma Beach."},{"day":3,"title":"Onward Transfer: From Jember to Tumpak Sewu Area","summary":"After breakfast at your Jember hotel and perhaps some free time, the journey continues in the afternoon. This route connects downtown Jember with the rural areas of Lumajang, setting you up in a prime location for your Tumpak Sewu Waterfall adventure the next day."},{"day":4,"title":"Mount Bromo and Return to Surabaya''s Civilization","summary":"The day begins with a magical sunrise over Mount Bromo. After a volcanic adventure and a hearty breakfast, we''ll drive you back down the mountains to Surabaya, concluding your adventure."},{"day":5,"title":"Convenient Delivery to Juanda Airport","summary":"After enjoying your final breakfast at the hotel, take advantage of some free time before we pick you up for a quiet and stress-free transfer to Juanda International Airport (SUB) for your onward flight."}],"title":"Day-by-day itinerary"},{"id":"requirements","title":"What you need to bring and know","bullets":["Moderate to good fitness","Printed passport for Ijen permit","Warm clothing (5–15°C)","Sturdy hiking shoes and water shoes","Rain jacket/poncho for waterfalls"]},{"id":"includes","title":"What is included","bullets":["Private transport: AC vehicle (MPV 1–3 guests, Minibus 4–11), driver, fuel, tolls, parking","Tour guides: English-speaking. Driver-guide for 1–3 pax; separate local guide at each destination for 4+","Mineral water: daily supply","Complimentary JVTO travel T-shirt (1 per participant)","Full assistance: arrival to final drop-off","Hotel accommodation: quality hotels, daily breakfast included","All entrance fees and permits","Meals as stated in itinerary","Private 4WD Jeep for Bromo sunrise tour","Ijen health screening: doctor check evening before trek (passport only required)","Trekking equipment: gas masks + trekking poles (Ijen); helmets at Madakaripura by local management","Ferry tickets: Ketapang Harbour → Gilimanuk Harbour (Bali)"]},{"id":"excludes","title":"What is not included","bullets":["International/domestic air tickets","Indonesian VISA (if applicable)","Travel insurance (recommended)","Meals not stated in itinerary (own expense)","Personal expenses: snacks, souvenirs, beverages (carry min IDR 500,000/person)","Tips for drivers and guides (at discretion)"]}],"cross_links":{"verify":"/verify-jvto","contact":"/contact","packing":"/travel-guide/packing-and-fitness","tours_hub":"/tours","ijen_health":"/travel-guide/ijen-health-screening","booking_info":"/travel-guide/booking-information"},"intro_paragraphs":["Adventure seekers, nature lovers, and those seeking iconic volcanic landscapes.","All-inclusive: private transport, accommodation, all entrance fees and permits, English-speaking guides, and meals as stated in the itinerary.","Official channels: Website https://javavolcano-touroperator.com • WhatsApp +6282244788833 • Email hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com."],"body_md":"# 5D4N Full Circuit Extended (Bali–Surabaya)\n\nPrivate 5D4N tour from Bali, covering kawah-ijen, papuma-beach, tumpak-sewu, mount-bromo.\n\nA medical health screening is mandatory for every guest before Kawah Ijen crater entry, per BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024 — included in the price.\n\n## Pricing (private, per person)\n- 2 pax: IDR 5,450,000 per person\n- 3 pax: IDR 5,250,000 per person\n- 4–5 pax: IDR 4,950,000 per person\n- 6–7 pax: IDR 4,650,000 per person\n- 8–10 pax: IDR 4,250,000 per person\n- 11–null pax: IDR 4,050,000 per person"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/tours/from-bali/ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-5d4n' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, varia