INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'live', '{"h1":"Best Time to Visit — East Java Destinations","body_md":"# Best Time to Visit — East Java Destinations\n\nThere is no universally bad time to visit East Java — but there is a best window for each destination, and knowing the seasonal patterns helps you choose dates that match what you are hoping to experience.\n\n---\n\n## Dry Season vs Wet Season — Overview\n\nEast Java has two main seasons:\n\n| Season | Approximate months | What to expect |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dry season** | April – October | Lower rainfall, clearer skies, better road and trail conditions. Recommended for Bromo and Ijen. |\n| **Wet season** | November – March | Higher rainfall, possible cloud cover at viewpoints, some trail conditions more variable. Canyon destinations remain popular. |\n\nThe key practical difference for volcano tours: Bromo and Ijen activities happen between late night and early morning — before the heavier rain that is more common later in the day. Weather is never fully predictable, but the dry season significantly improves the probability of clear conditions at both viewpoints.\n\n---\n\n## Kawah Ijen\n\n**Best season**: April – October (dry season)\n\nThe Ijen night hike begins around midnight; the Blue Fire viewing window closes around dawn. Cloud cover and rainfall are lower in the dry season, which improves visibility at the crater floor and the rim viewpoint.\n\nBlue Fire is a natural phenomenon subject to weather and gas activity — clear skies are helpful but not the only variable. Gas venting direction and wind conditions also affect visibility, independent of rainfall.\n\nIjen is also subject to closure on the **first Friday of every month** (scheduled BBKSDA closure) and may close additionally when gas levels or safety conditions require it. Check bbksdajatim.org for current announcements.\n\nTemperatures at the Ijen crater rim: 10–15°C (50–59°F) at the midnight departure window.\n\n---\n\n## Mount Bromo\n\n**Best season**: April – October (dry season)\n\nBromo''s main activity is the pre-dawn sunrise at Penanjakan viewpoint (2,770 m) and the jeep traverse across the Sea of Sand caldera floor. The dry season gives the best chance of clear skies for the sunrise view across the Tengger caldera.\n\nThe annual Kasada festival (date varies by lunar calendar) falls in the dry season and can restrict or crowd Bromo crater access for a short period each year. JVTO activates its Plan-B SOP for bookings during this window. Contact us when you enquire and we will check whether your dates overlap.\n\nTemperatures at Bromo viewpoints pre-dawn: 5–15°C (41–59°F). Warm layers are essential.\n\n---\n\n## Tumpak Sewu\n\n**Year-round destination.** Tumpak Sewu is a wet-terrain experience at any time of year — the canyon descent involves ropes, handholds, and river crossings regardless of season. During the wet season (November–March), water flow at the falls is typically higher and more dramatic. During the dry season, the trail is somewhat less slippery.\n\nMany guests specifically choose the wet season for Tumpak Sewu because the waterfall volume is at its peak. Either season works; the choice depends on whether you prioritise dramatic water volume or more manageable trail conditions.\n\n---\n\n## Madakaripura\n\n**Year-round destination.** Madakaripura canyon is a wading and canyon experience in all conditions. You will get wet regardless of season. Wet season visits may see higher water levels in the stream approach; dry season visits are more predictable but still involve water.\n\n---\n\n## Booking Timing\n\nFor dry-season departures (April–October), particularly June through August, dates fill earlier than the rest of the year. If you are targeting a specific departure date in peak season, we recommend enquiring at least 4–6 weeks in advance.\n\nFor all bookings, the standard deposit is 20% of the total. Full payment deadlines: card no later than 5 days before Day 1; bank wire or Wise no later than 3 days before Day 1.\n\nTo check availability for your preferred dates, contact JVTO via WhatsApp (+62 822 4478 8833) or email (hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com).","source":"llm-wiki:pages/travel-guide/best-time-to-visit"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/best-time-to-visit' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
