INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Bromo & Ijen Itinerary Guide — How Many Days Do You Need?","body_md":"# Bromo & Ijen Itinerary Guide — How Many Days Do You Need?\n\nJVTO operates 16 private tour packages across East Java. The right one depends on how many days you have, which destinations matter to you, and where you start. This guide breaks down what each duration actually covers.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Comparison\n\n| Duration | What you see | Starting from (2 pax) | Best for |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1D1N | Bromo sunrise only | IDR 1,550,000 | Short on time, already near Surabaya |\n| 2D1N | Bromo + Madakaripura OR Ijen only | IDR 2,300,000 | Weekend trip, single destination |\n| 3D2N | Ijen + Bromo + Madakaripura | IDR 3,570,000 | Classic combination, most popular |\n| 4D3N | Add Papuma Beach + Tumpak Sewu OR extra rest day | IDR 4,450,000 | Full experience without rushing |\n| 5D4N | Full East Java circuit | IDR 5,050,000 | Comprehensive, includes all 5 destinations |\n| 6D5N | Grand tour + Malang city | IDR 6,050,000 | Maximum coverage, urban + volcanic |\n\n---\n\n## 1-Day: Bromo Midnight Experience\n\n**Package**: `bromo-1d1n` (Surabaya origin only)\n\nDepart Surabaya late at night. Jeep to Penanjakan viewpoint for Milky Way and sunrise. Descend to Sea of Sand, walk to crater. Breakfast included. Return to Surabaya by midday.\n\n**What you miss**: Ijen, waterfalls, the slower pace of a multi-day trip.\n**Who picks this**: Business travelers with one free night, cruise ship passengers, anyone already staying in Surabaya.\n\n---\n\n## 2-Day: Single Destination Focus\n\nTwo options:\n\n**Bromo + Madakaripura** (`bromo-2d1n`): Day 1 transfer to Bromo area. Day 2 sunrise + Madakaripura waterfall canyon trek + return to Surabaya. No Ijen.\n\n**Ijen Blue Fire** (`ijen-2d1n`): Day 1 transfer to Bondowoso, dinner, health screening. Day 2 midnight Ijen climb, blue fire window, crater lake at sunrise, return to Surabaya.\n\n**Key difference**: Bromo is a jeep-based sunrise experience. Ijen is a physical night hike with volcanic gas exposure — requires medical screening.\n\n---\n\n## 3-Day: The Classic Combination\n\nThe most-booked duration. Two route directions:\n\n**Ijen → Bromo → Madakaripura** (`ijen-bromo-madakaripura-3d2n`, SUB→SUB):\n- Day 1: Surabaya → Bondowoso. Health screening. Dinner.\n- Day 2: Midnight Ijen climb → descent → lunch → overland transfer to Bromo area (~5 hours).\n- Day 3: Bromo sunrise → Madakaripura waterfall → return to Surabaya.\n\n**Bromo → Madakaripura → Ijen** (`bromo-madakaripura-ijen-3d2n`, SUB→Bali):\n- Day 1: Surabaya → Bromo area staging.\n- Day 2: Bromo sunrise → Madakaripura → transfer east to Bondowoso. Health screening.\n- Day 3: Midnight Ijen climb → Ketapang ferry → finish in Bali.\n\n**Which direction?** If you fly into Surabaya and out of Bali (or vice versa), pick the route that matches your flight sequence. The SUB→Bali direction avoids backtracking.\n\n---\n\n## 4-Day: Full Circuit or Relaxed Pace\n\nThree variants:\n\n**Ijen + Bromo + Madakaripura + Surabaya finish** (`ijen-bromo-madakaripura-4d3n`): Same as 3-day but adds a Surabaya city overnight on Day 3, with Day 4 as a clean airport transfer. Suited for late-departing flights.\n\n**Ijen + Papuma + Tumpak Sewu + Bromo** (`ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-4d3n`): Adds Papuma Beach and Tumpak Sewu waterfall. The full East Java circuit in 4 days — volcanoes, beach, and waterfall canyon.\n\n**Tumpak Sewu + Bromo + Ijen → Bali** (`tumpak-sewu-bromo-ijen-4d3n`): Starts with Tumpak Sewu, ends with Ijen crossing to Bali. Different route direction for different flight logistics.\n\n---\n\n## 5-Day: Comprehensive Coverage\n\n**Full circuit** (`ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-5d4n`): All five destinations — Ijen, Papuma Beach, Tumpak Sewu, Bromo, plus a Surabaya finish. Extra day vs the 4-day gives more breathing room at each stop.\n\n**Ijen + Bromo + Madakaripura + Malang** (`ijen-bromo-madakaripura-malang-5d4n`): Swaps the coastal/waterfall segment for Malang city and Batu area exploration. Day 4 shifts away from mountain rhythm — city, food, and culture.\n\n---\n\n## 6-Day: The Grand Tour\n\n**Grand East Java** (`ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-malang-6d5n`): Everything. Ijen, Papuma, Tumpak Sewu, Bromo, Malang, and Surabaya. Six days covers every JVTO destination with room for rest between volcanic segments.\n\n---\n\n## Transfer Times Between Destinations\n\n| Segment | Drive time |\n|---|---|\n| Surabaya → Bromo (Cemoro Lawang) | ~3 hours |\n| Ijen (Paltuding) → Surabaya | 5–6 hours |\n| Tumpak Sewu → Bromo | 3–4 hours |\n| Bali → Ijen (Banyuwangi side) | 5–7 hours (includes ferry) |\n\nAll transfers are in your private vehicle with a dedicated driver. No shared transport.\n\n---\n\n## Recurring Patterns You''ll See\n\n**Ijen staging**: Arrive evening → health screening at hotel → midnight departure to Paltuding → 1.5–2 hour ascent → blue fire window → crater lake at sunrise → descent.\n\n**Bromo sunrise**: 01:00–02:00 departure → jeep to Penanjakan → Milky Way window → sunrise (~05:30) → descent to Sea of Sand → crater walk → breakfast at hotel.\n\nThese sequences are fixed by natural timing (sunrise, gas conditions). The packages differ in what comes before and after.\n\n---\n\n## How to Choose\n\n1. **How many days do you have?** The comparison table above narrows it immediately.\n2. **Where do you fly in/out?** If you arrive Surabaya and depart Bali (or reverse), pick a cross-island route to avoid backtracking.\n3. **Do you want Ijen?** 12 of 16 packages include Ijen. If you do, medical screening is mandatory and included.\n4. **Beach or city?** 5-day has two variants — coastal (Papuma) or urban (Malang). Pick your preference.\n\nAll packages are private — schedule adjustments happen in real time with your crew.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Receipt\n| Claim | Value used | SSOT source | Last verified | Drift risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Package count | 16 (12+4) | packages-overview.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| bromo-1d1n 2-pax price | 1,550,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| ijen-2d1n 2-pax price | 2,300,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| 3d2n SUB 2-pax price | 3,570,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| 4d3n expedition 2-pax price | 4,450,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| 5d4n full 2-pax price | 5,050,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| 6d5n grand 2-pax price | 6,050,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| SUB→Bromo transfer | ~3 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| Ijen→SUB transfer | 5–6 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| Tumpak Sewu→Bromo | 3–4 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| Bali→Ijen | 5–7 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/bromo-ijen-itinerary-guide' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/bromo-vs-ijen-comparison' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Mount Bromo vs Mount Ijen: Which Volcano Tour is Best for You?","body_md":"# Mount Bromo vs Mount Ijen: Which Volcano Tour is Best for You?\n\nChoosing between East Java’s two iconic active volcanoes depends on your physical fitness level, what landscapes you want to see, and your overall travel timeline. While Mount Bromo offers a dramatic, lunar-like caldera vista at sunrise with minimal physical exertion, Mount Ijen presents a demanding night expedition to see the rare Blue Fire and the world’s largest acidic crater lake.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Quick Comparison Table\n\n| Feature | Mount Bromo | Mount Ijen |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Elevation** | 2,329 m | 2,386 m |\n| **Primary Differentiator** | Vast caldera, volcanic sea of sand, active smoking crater | Pre-dawn Blue Fire, acidic turquoise lake, sulfur miners |\n| **Physical Difficulty** | **Easy to Moderate** (mostly paved stair climb) | **Moderate to Demanding** (steep dirt/rock trail hike) |\n| **Hike Distance** | ~1.5 km (flat walk + 250 concrete stairs) | ~3 km one-way (~90 min steep ascent) |\n| **Optional Descent** | None | ~700 m steep rocky path down to crater floor |\n| **Departure Time** | 03:00 WIB (from Bromo hotels) | 00:00 WIB (from Banyuwangi/Bondowoso) |\n| **Health Certificate** | Not required | **Yes** (BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024 — mandatory for every guest) |\n| **Required Safety Gear** | Dust mask (for volcanic sand) | Professional gas mask & headlamp |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Mount Bromo: The Easiest Volcano Adventure\n\nMount Bromo sits within the massive Tengger Caldera at 2,329 meters. It is famous for its ethereal sunrise scenery, where the active Bromo crater and surrounding volcanic peaks emerge from a sea of morning mist.\n\n### The Experience\nA private 4WD jeep takes you across the \"Sea of Sand\" (Pasir Berbisik) to Penanjakan or King Kong Hill viewpoints. After the sunrise, you travel across the caldera floor to the foot of Bromo. You can walk or hire a horse to cross the flat sand field before climbing 250 concrete steps to look directly into the active smoking crater.\n\n### Who is it for?\nBromo is highly recommended for families, older travelers, and those seeking dramatic volcanic views without a strenuous mountain trek. \n\n---\n\n## 3. Mount Ijen: The Demanding Night Expedition\n\nMount Ijen (2,386 m) is a stark, rugged environment. The climb is conducted in the dark of night to witness the Blue Fire—an igniting sulfuric gas phenomenon on the crater floor.\n\n### The Experience\nThe climb begins at 02:00 WIB from the Paltuding trailhead. The path is a steep, unpaved 3 km dirt track that takes roughly 90 minutes to ascend. To see the Blue Fire, you must descend a steep, rocky, single-file path 700 meters into the crater. Here, you will wear professional chemical gas masks to filter out dense sulfur dioxide fumes. At sunrise, you see the turquoise-colored acidic lake (pH ≈ 0) and meet the local sulfur miners carrying 80 kg loads up the crater wall.\n\n> **Safety & Regulatory Note**: Blue Fire is a natural phenomenon subject to weather and gas activity; sightings are never guaranteed. Additionally, a health certificate is mandatory for every guest before Kawah Ijen crater entry, per BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024. JVTO coordinates the clinic screening workflow with our licensed medical officer when BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024 regulations require it.\n\n### Who is it for?\nIjen is suited for active travelers with good physical conditioning, stable footing, and no history of severe cardiovascular or respiratory issues (such as asthma).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Logistics & Starting Points\n\n- **From Surabaya**: Bromo is a 3–4 hour drive, making it suitable for short weekend trips. Ijen lies much further east (a 6-hour drive), so a combined Bromo-Ijen tour requires a minimum of 3 days.\n- **From Bali**: Ijen is highly accessible from Bali via a short ferry crossing from Gilimanuk to Ketapang (Banyuwangi). Bali-origin packages typically cross into Java on Day 1, hike Ijen on Day 2, and Bromo on Day 3.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Trust JVTO for Your Volcano Tour\n\nJVTO operates 100% private tours with dedicated AC vehicles, expert guides, and private 4WD Bromo jeeps. We coordinate all tickets, local screening checks, and provide professional gas masks for your safety.\n\nPT Java Volcano Rendezvous · NIB 1102230032918 · Trustpilot 4.8 / 5 (51 reviews, verified 2026-05-09)","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/bromo-vs-ijen-comparison' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/private-vs-shared-tour-comparison' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Private vs. Shared Volcano Tours: Why Execution Control Matters","body_md":"# Private vs. Shared Volcano Tours: Why Execution Control Matters\n\nWhen planning a tour to Mount Bromo and Mount Ijen, you will choose between a **100% private tour** and a **shared tour (open trip)**. While shared tours attract budget-conscious travelers with low base rates, they require significant compromises in safety, vehicle comfort, and schedule flexibility.\n\nHere is an analysis of how a private JVTO tour compares to typical shared tours in East Java.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Key Comparison\n\n| Feature | Private Tour (JVTO) | Shared Tour (Open Trip) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Vehicle Occupancy** | Dedicated vehicle for your group only | Shared van with 10–14 strangers |\n| **Pacing & Schedule** | Flexible. You decide when to stop, rest, or eat | Rigid. Fixed departure times; no adjustments |\n| **Dedicated Guide** | Private guide assigned to your party | 1 guide responsible for 15–20 travelers |\n| **Safety Integration** | Direct health-check coordination and individual gear checks | Mass screening at the trailhead; no individual tracking |\n| **Pricing Model** | **All-inclusive**. Zero surprise payments. | Low entry price; hidden jeep or entry fees |\n| **Rescheduling & Credit** | 100% Lifetime Package Credit (if cancelled ≥48h before) | Non-refundable; immediate forfeiture |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Pacing Control: The Key to Volcanic Safety\n\nHiking active volcanoes requires physical endurance. Kawah Ijen''s night ascent is a steep 3 km climb followed by a rocky descent into the sulfur crater.\n\n- **On a Shared Tour**: The group must move at a uniform pace. If you need to rest, you risk being left behind by the guide who must keep the entire group on schedule to catch the sunrise.\n- **On a Private JVTO Tour**: Your guide monitors your group’s breathing, heart rate, and fatigue. You can pause to rest, adjust your pace, or decide to skip the crater descent without affecting anyone else. Your safety is our primary focus.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Vehicle Comfort and Overland Fatigue\n\nBromo-Ijen routes require 4 to 6 hours of overland driving between cities like Surabaya, Probolinggo, Banyuwangi, and Malang.\n\n- **On a Shared Tour**: Vans are packed to maximum capacity to cover operational costs. You will spend hours waiting at fixed pick-up points for other guests, and rest stops are strictly scheduled.\n- **On a Private JVTO Tour**: Your group gets a dedicated AC vehicle. We allocate an MPV for 2–3 guests and a spacious Toyota Hiace for larger groups. You can request restroom breaks, stop for local food (like East Java durians), or pause to stretch whenever you choose.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Transparent Inclusions vs. Hidden Charges\n\nA common complaint in shared tours is the \"add-on fee\" structure.\n\n- **Shared tours** often exclude national park entrance fees (which cost up to IDR 220,000/person for foreign tourists on weekends), charge extra for gas mask rentals at Ijen, or require local cash payments to board the Bromo 4WD jeep.\n- **JVTO packages** are transparently all-inclusive. Private AC transport, dedicated guide and driver, entrance fees, private 4WD Bromo jeep, safety gear (respirators and poles), medical screening coordination, daily water, and accommodation are bundled into the price. \"Read the Rulebook Before You Book\" is our policy.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rescheduling and Cancellation Flexibility\n\nVolcanic activity, flight delays, and personal health issues can disrupt travel plans.\n\n- **Shared tours** generally operate a strict \"no refund, no reschedule\" policy because seats are sold individually and departures depend on filling the van.\n- **JVTO''s booking terms** provide industry-leading protection. If you cancel your tour at least 48 hours before Day 1, 100% of the eligible booking value is converted into a Lifetime Package Credit. This credit has no expiration date, is fully transferable, and can be used to book any JVTO route. We also offer one free reschedule with 48 hours'' notice.\n\n---\n\nPT Java Volcano Rendezvous · NIB 1102230032918 · Trustpilot 4.8 / 5 (51 reviews, verified 2026-05-09)","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/private-vs-shared-tour-comparison' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/surabaya-vs-bali-starting-point' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Starting from Surabaya vs Bali","body_md":"# Starting from Surabaya vs Bali\n\nJVTO operates 16 private tour packages — 12 departing from Surabaya, 4 from Bali. The destinations are the same volcanoes and waterfalls. The difference is logistics: where you begin, which direction you travel, and how long the first transfer takes.\n\n---\n\n## Side-by-Side Comparison\n\n| Factor | Surabaya origin | Bali origin |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Packages available** | 12 | 4 |\n| **Duration range** | 1D1N to 6D5N | 3D2N to 5D4N |\n| **First transfer** | SUB → Bromo (~3h) or SUB → Bondowoso (~5h) | Bali → Banyuwangi (~5–7h, includes ferry) |\n| **Ijen staging hotel** | Riverside Homestay, Bondowoso | Luminor Hotel, Banyuwangi |\n| **Ferry crossing** | Only if ending in Bali | Required on Day 1 (Gilimanuk → Ketapang) |\n| **Typical route direction** | East (Ijen) → West (Bromo) → return SUB | West (Ijen from Banyuwangi) → West (Bromo) → finish SUB |\n| **Cross-island option** | SUB → Bali (`bromo-madakaripura-ijen-3d2n`) | Bali → SUB (all 4 packages end in Surabaya) |\n| **3D2N price (2 pax)** | IDR 3,570,000 | IDR 4,050,000 |\n\n---\n\n## When to Start from Surabaya\n\n**Choose Surabaya if:**\n- You fly into Juanda Airport (SUB) — most domestic flights from Jakarta, Singapore, and Kuala Lumpur land here\n- You want the widest selection — 12 packages vs 4, including short trips (1D1N, 2D1N) not available from Bali\n- You plan to return to Surabaya after the tour\n- You want to add Malang city or Taman Safari Prigen — these are Surabaya-origin exclusives\n\n**Surabaya advantage**: Shorter first transfer to Bromo (~3 hours). If your package starts with Bromo, you reach the staging hotel by afternoon with a comfortable 09:00 pick-up.\n\n**12 Surabaya packages by duration:**\n\n| Duration | Packages | Destinations covered |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1D1N | 1 | Bromo only |\n| 2D1N | 2 | Bromo+Madakaripura OR Ijen only |\n| 3D2N | 3 | Ijen+Bromo+Madakaripura (incl. 1 cross-island to Bali) |\n| 4D3N | 3 | Add Papuma+Tumpak Sewu or relaxed pace |\n| 5D4N | 2 | Full circuit or Malang extension |\n| 6D5N | 1 | Grand tour (all destinations + Malang) |\n\n---\n\n## When to Start from Bali\n\n**Choose Bali if:**\n- You are already in Bali and want to add East Java volcanoes without flying to Surabaya first\n- You prefer a one-way overland journey — all 4 Bali packages end in Surabaya (no Bali-to-Bali round trip except `bali/bromo-ijen-3d2n` which returns to Bali)\n- Your flight home departs from Surabaya\n\n**Bali trade-off**: The first day is mostly transfer. Bali → Gilimanuk → Ketapang ferry → Banyuwangi takes 5–7 hours depending on traffic and ferry timing. You arrive at the Ijen staging hotel (Luminor Hotel, Banyuwangi) in the evening.\n\n**4 Bali packages:**\n\n| Slug | Duration | 2-pax price | Ends in |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `bromo-ijen-3d2n` | 3D2N | IDR 4,050,000 | Bali (round trip) |\n| `ijen-bromo-madakaripura-3d2n` | 3D2N | IDR 4,050,000 | Surabaya |\n| `ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-4d3n` | 4D3N | IDR 4,900,000 | Surabaya |\n| `ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-5d4n` | 5D4N | IDR 5,450,000 | Surabaya |\n\n---\n\n## Price Difference Explained\n\nBali-origin packages cost more than the equivalent Surabaya-origin package. The difference covers the Gilimanuk–Ketapang ferry crossing and the longer first-day transfer from Bali to East Java. The tour content (destinations, hotels, crew, inclusions) is identical.\n\n**Example — 3D2N Ijen + Bromo + Madakaripura:**\n- Surabaya origin: IDR 3,570,000/person (2 pax)\n- Bali origin: IDR 4,050,000/person (2 pax)\n- Difference: IDR 480,000 — covers ferry + ~2 extra hours of driving\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Island Routes\n\nIf you fly into one city and out of the other, pick the cross-island variant to avoid backtracking:\n\n| Scenario | Package |\n|---|---|\n| Fly in SUB → fly out Bali | `bromo-madakaripura-ijen-3d2n` (SUB→Bali, 3D2N) |\n| Fly in SUB → fly out Bali | `tumpak-sewu-bromo-ijen-4d3n` (SUB→Bali, 4D3N) |\n| Fly in Bali → fly out SUB | Any of the 4 Bali-origin packages (all end in Surabaya, except `bromo-ijen-3d2n` which returns to Bali) |\n| Fly in SUB → fly out SUB | Most Surabaya packages (round-trip) |\n| Fly in Bali → fly out Bali | `bali/bromo-ijen-3d2n` only (3D2N round-trip) |\n\n---\n\n## Transfer Time Summary\n\n| Segment | Time |\n|---|---|\n| Surabaya → Bromo (Cemoro Lawang) | ~3 hours |\n| Surabaya → Bondowoso (Ijen staging) | ~5 hours |\n| Bali → Banyuwangi (Ijen staging, via ferry) | 5–7 hours |\n| Ijen area → Bromo area (overland) | ~5 hours |\n| Tumpak Sewu → Bromo | 3–4 hours |\n| Bromo → Surabaya | ~3 hours |\n\nAll transfers in your private vehicle. No shared transport, no public bus connections.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Receipt\n| Claim | Value used | SSOT source | Last verified | Drift risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SUB packages | 12 | packages-overview.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| Bali packages | 4 | packages-overview.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| SUB→Bromo time | ~3 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| Bali→Ijen time | 5–7 hours | operational-facts.md | 2026-05-16 | Low |\n| 3d2n SUB 2-pax | 3,570,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| 3d2n Bali 2-pax | 4,050,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| Bali 4d3n 2-pax | 4,900,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| Bali 5d4n 2-pax | 5,450,000 | packages-full-pricing.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| Ijen staging (SUB) | Riverside Homestay Bondowoso | packages-itineraries.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| Ijen staging (Bali) | Luminor Hotel Banyuwangi | packages-itineraries.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |\n| Bromo hotel | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo | packages-itineraries.md | 2026-05-12 | Low |","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/surabaya-vs-bali-starting-point' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
