INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs, editable) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"What to Pack for Your Bromo & Ijen Volcano Tour","body_md":"# What to Pack for Your Bromo & Ijen Volcano Tour\n\nEast Java’s volcanic terrain demands careful packing. In a single day, you will experience temperatures near freezing (5°C to 10°C) before dawn at high altitudes, followed by warm daytime sunshine (20°C to 25°C), and wet canyon trails if your tour includes Madakaripura or Tumpak Sewu waterfalls. \n\nHere is the definitive packing checklist verified by the JVTO operations team.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Clothing Layering System\n\nDo not pack a single heavy winter coat. Instead, pack layers you can easily shed as the sun rises and you generate body heat during the climb.\n\n- **Base Layer**: A moisture-wicking thermal top and bottom (merino wool or synthetic). Avoid cotton, which traps sweat and chills your body.\n- **Mid-Layer**: A fleece jacket or lightweight down jacket to trap warm air.\n- **Outer Shell**: A windproof and water-resistant jacket. Wind chill on the Penanjakan Bromo sunrise deck and the Ijen crater rim can be severe.\n- **Trekking Pants**: Long, lightweight, stretchy pants. Avoid denim jeans, which are heavy and restrict movement on steep trails.\n- **Warm Accessories**: A wool beanie to cover your ears, lightweight windproof gloves, and a neck gaiter or scarf.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Footwear: Grip is Critical\n\nBoth volcanoes feature loose gravel, sand, and steep slopes. Slipping is the most common cause of minor injuries.\n\n- **Hiking Shoes**: Sturdy trail-running shoes or mid-cut hiking boots with a deep tread (Vibram or rubber lugs). Paved and unpaved trails are slippery when covered in dry volcanic ash or wet mud.\n- **Socks**: Merino wool or synthetic hiking socks to prevent blisters. Pack a spare pair.\n- **Canyon Sandals**: If your tour includes Madakaripura or Tumpak Sewu, bring strap-on water shoes or adventure sandals. You will be wading through water streams.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Volcano Safety Gear: What JVTO Provides\n\nJVTO coordinates your safety equipment so you don''t have to carry heavy gear across Indonesia. The following items are provided at the trailhead:\n\n- **Professional Gas Mask**: Sanitized half-face industrial respirators with chemical cartridges to filter out sulfur dioxide (SO2) gases at Ijen.\n- **Trekking Poles**: Adjustable poles to assist with balance on Ijen''s steep unpaved trail and the optional crater descent.\n- **Headlamp**: LED headlamps for the midnight ascent of Kawah Ijen.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Personal Items & Protection\n\n- **Sunglasses**: The sun reflecting off Ijen''s white volcanic ash and sulfur rocks can be blinding.\n- **Sunscreen & Lip Balm**: High-altitude sun is intense, and dry volcanic wind quickly cracks lips.\n- **Rain Poncho**: A lightweight raincoat is essential. For Madakaripura Waterfall, you will walk through heavy canyon spray and *will* get wet.\n- **Personal Medications**: Bring your own prescription medicines. \n  > *Note: A health certificate is mandatory for every guest before Kawah Ijen crater entry, per BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024. JVTO coordinates the clinic screening workflow with our medical officer under BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024. If you have a history of asthma or heart conditions, consult a physician before booking.*\n\n---\n\n## 5. Travel Logistics checklist\n\n- **Original Passport**: Required at the Kawah Ijen entry checkpoint and hotel check-ins.\n- **Cash in IDR**: JVTO tours are all-inclusive, but you will need Indonesian Rupiah (IDR) for tips, personal snacks, and souvenirs. \n- **Travel Voucher**: A digital copy of your JVTO E-Voucher saved on your phone.\n\n---\n\nPT Java Volcano Rendezvous · NIB 1102230032918 · Trustpilot 4.8 / 5 (51 reviews, verified 2026-05-09)","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], false FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/travel-guide/what-to-pack-bromo-ijen' ON CONFLICT (page_id, sort_order) DO UPDATE SET section_type = EXCLUDED.section_type, variant = EXCLUDED.variant, content = EXCLUDED.content, entity_refs = EXCLUDED.entity_refs, asset_refs = EXCLUDED.asset_refs WHERE page_sections.editable IS NOT TRUE;
